<title>SPAIN: Bankinter to split shares 3-for-1.</title>
<headline>Bankinter to split shares 3-for-1.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Bankinter said on Tuesday it would split its shares three-for-one, reducing the nominal value of each to 500 pesetas from 1,500.</p>
<p>The move is subject to shareholder approval.  </p>
<p>&quot;The nominal reduction of shares to 500 pesetas from 1,500 will be achieved by splitting each share into three, thereby tripling the number of shares in circulation,&quot; a bank spokeswoman said.</p>
</text>
